# seed/ng/tests/ir/cases: ngcheck, ngas, ngdis and ng ir-copy expectations, run by seed/ng/gate-ir.om.
# Every refusal is judged by its whole stderr line (IR.md s10, s11) and an empty stdout; an acceptance by
# the whole ngcheck line "ACCEPT <sha256> fns=F blocks=B ops=O" with F, B, O counted from the fixture text.
# ng ir-copy sees every unit: classes 10, 11, 12, 14, 15, 23, 27 must give ngcheck's refusal line, any
# other verdict the same bytes back (or, when ngcheck refuses, a refusal of its own).
# T NAME EXIT OFFSET       NAME.oir: ngas exit 0, ngdis(ngas(t)) == t, ngcheck exit and offset (- when 0)
# S NAME LINE              NAME.oir: ngas refuses, exit 3, at LINE
# M BASE POS BYTE EXIT OFF  BASE.oir assembled, byte POS set to BYTE: ngcheck and ngdis exit EXIT at OFF
# C BASE LEN EXIT OFF       ... cut to LEN bytes
# A BASE BYTE EXIT OFF      ... BYTE appended
# D EXIT OFF                stdin is a directory: ngcheck, ngdis and ng exit EXIT at OFF, ngas exit EXIT
# G GEN TOOL EXIT OFF       generated input (gate-ir.om gt_gen): full = a unit of exactly 16777216 bytes,
#                          over = full + 1 byte, types = 65537 populated type entries; tyN, gl65537,
#                          fn65537, bl65537, fp65537, bp65537 = text with N (65537) types, globals,
#                          functions, blocks in one function, function or block parameters. TOOL c ngcheck,
#                          d ngdis, n ng ir-copy, a ngas (OFF is a line), r ngas then ngdis gives the text back
#                          x ngrun FILE (refusals only)
# R NAME                    NAME.oir accepted by ngcheck and run by ngrun; NAME.om compiled by OMC and run:
#                          exit status, stdout and stderr equal (D9 differential, IR.md s7 semantics)
# Q N                       ngrand seeds 1..N: ngcheck ACCEPT (whole line), ngas(ngdis(b)) == b, ngrun ends
#                          cleanly (exit 0..63 with 0 or 8 stdout bytes, 64..95, or a trap 101..114)
#                          and the optimizer passes on each seed (as O below)
# N NAME EXIT OFF          NAME.oir run by `ngrun FILE 1000000` (a step budget): exit EXIT, empty stdout,
#                          stderr empty or, for 124 / 126, "ngrun: step limit at OFF" / "ngrun: access
#                          outside storage at OFF"
# K SEED STATUS             ngrand shrink SEED STATUS with ngrun as the predicate: the result is accepted,
#                          ngrun exits STATUS on it, it is smaller than SEED's unit, its tape replays it
# O NAME [ROW]              seed/ng/tests/opt/NAME.oir through `@ng opt`: exit 0, stderr empty, ngcheck's
#                          whole ACCEPT line, ngas(ngdis(out)) == out, ngrun before == after (exit, stdout,
#                          stderr; one decimal clock line each side counts as equal), `@ng opt-count` of
#                          the output a fixed point; prints "ok O NAME fns=.. loops=.. inloop=A->B ...".
#                          ROW, when given (" fns=.. preheaders=.."), must equal `@ng opt-count` of the
#                          input after its "opt", so each pass is pinned to do what it did, no less
#                          ("FAIL ...: opt counts differ, got ..." otherwise)
# L NAME [ROW]              as O, for a long-running unit: skipped under a mutant
